{
  "_comment": "Golden contract for the pure reminder core (src/core/reminders.cjs::dueReminders). Input is the opportunity rows as stored — a nullable `deadline_at` UTC instant, a `confirmed` flag and a `reminders_sent` list of already-fired lead times — plus the instant, zone and lead times as explicit arguments. `expect` is the exact reminder list, in order. Days remaining are counted in calendar days in `zone`, not in UTC, so a deadline late on the local day is not one day nearer just because UTC has already rolled over. Replaces the Notion-shaped deadline-page contract of the n8n build: deadlines are a scalar on the opportunity now, and idempotency lives in `reminders_sent` rather than in an external data table.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "deadline_seven_days_out_matches_lead_time",
      "now": "2026-07-06T18:00:00.000Z",
      "zone": "America/Mexico_City",
      "lead_times": [30, 7, 1],
      "opportunities": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "PhD in Trustworthy AI",
          "confirmed": true,
          "deadline_at": "2026-07-13T23:59:00.000Z",
          "reminders_sent": []
        }
      ],
      "expect": [
        {
          "opportunity_id": 1,
          "title": "PhD in Trustworthy AI",
          "lead_time": 7,
          "days_remaining": 7,
          "deadline_at": "2026-07-13T23:59:00.000Z"
        }
      ]
    },
